Attribution granularity
------------------------
Attribution for this port is carried at two levels:

  - This NOTICE file records the project-level relationship to upstream:
    what was ported, from where, and under what license.
  - Individual Go source files that port a specific Java class or file
    carry a `// Ported from <upstream-path> (DSS 6.5.RC1).` header comment
    identifying the exact upstream source file that code was derived
    from. Those per-file headers are the authoritative, file-level
    attribution record and must not be removed.

For the full mapping of upstream Maven modules to Go packages see
docs/migrating-from-java/index.md; for the porting conventions applied
throughout, see dss/PORTING.md in this repository.

